  "live_records": {
    "q-278482": {
      "dom_id": "step-q278482",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14134399/assets/19611e305d49d136f0a79189773b712243ec12f957fe16efca22ec2812393bd8.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(0,-2),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=5,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=3.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-0)^{2}}{{5}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-2))^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{9} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
