    "q-70482": {
      "dom_id": "step-q70482",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14134399/assets/a9278747563bf79a79e5633f2fae6d97a6ba021c38e8238ef9d22d1396df0be6.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(-2,-2),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=4,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=2.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-(-2))^{2}}{{4}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-2))^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
